   = \n| death_date        = <!-- {{Death date and age|YYYY|MM|DD|YYYY|MM|DD}} (death date first) -->\n| death_place       = \n| genre             = [[Contemporary R&B|R&B]]\n| occupation        = Singer, songwriter\n| years_active      = <!-- YYYY–YYYY (or –present) -->\n| label             = Finesse Records\n| associated_acts   = \n| website           = <!-- {{URL|example.com}} or {{Official URL}} -->\n| module            = \n| module2           = \n| module3           = \n}}\n'''Mariana de Miguel''' (born 1996),{{r|pacific|spin}} better known as '''Girl Ultra''', is a Mexican [[Contemporary R&B|R&B]] artist.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.vice.com/es/article/hormonas-de-21-anos-una-charla-con-girl-ultra/|title=Hormonas de 21 años: Una charla con Girl Ultra|last=López|first=Mixar|date=2017-03-09|website=Noisey|language=es|access-date=2019-04-01}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://remezcla.com/features/music/girl-ultra-boys-ep-interview/|title=Meet Girl Ultra, a Bleeding-Heart R&B Diva From Mexico City|date=2017-04-25|website=Remezcla|language=en-US|access-date=2019-03-09}}</ref> She signed to Mexican label Finesse Records in 2016<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://fierce.wearemitu.com/entertainment/up-next-girl-ultra-mexican-baby-girl-rb-espanol/|title=Up Next: Meet Girl Ultra, The Mexican Baby Girl Of R&B En Español|date=2018-10-09|website=Fierce|language=en-US|access-date=2019-03-09}}</ref> and released her debut EP, ''Boys'', in 2017. ''Boys'' includes a Spanish language cover of [[Daniel Caesar]] track \"[[Get You (Daniel Caesar song)|Get You]]\". She released her second EP, ''Adiós'', in 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.beatburguer.com/manual-de-los-adioses-por-girl-ultra-adios-ep/|title=Manual de los adioses, por Girl Ultra|date=2018-03-22|website=Beatburguer|language=es|access-date=2019-04-01}}</ref>"}}}]}]}}}}
